{
 "duration": 25.03,
 "lines": [
  {
   "text": "Ryan wore his heaviest coat on a frosty November morning.",
   "start": 0.3,
   "end": 3.69
  },
  {
   "text": "On the first climb he was sweating, so he took it off.",
   "start": 3.89,
   "end": 6.419
  },
  {
   "text": "Minutes later he froze in a damp T-shirt.",
   "start": 6.619,
   "end": 8.97
  },
  {
   "text": "Here's the fix. Dress in thin layers.",
   "start": 9.32,
   "end": 11.587
  },
  {
   "text": "A base layer that wicks sweat, a fleece for warmth, and a wind or rain shell on top.",
   "start": 11.787,
   "end": 16.651
  },
  {
   "text": "Too warm? Take one off. Cold at the break? Add it back.",
   "start": 16.851,
   "end": 20.12
  },
  {
   "text": "Ryan stayed comfortable all morning.",
   "start": 20.52,
   "end": 22.398
  },
  {
   "text": "Save this before your next cold hike.",
   "start": 22.798,
   "end": 24.83
  }
 ],
